    "finishStory": {
      "markedParagraph": "At Mount [SINAI], God reminded the Israelites that he had [RESCUED] them from slavery in Egypt. He gave them [ten] commandments and later wrote them on two stone [TABLETS] for Moses. The first command told them to worship no other [GODS]. The second said not to worship [IDOLS]. They were to honor God’s [NAME] and [REST] on the Sabbath. God told them to honor their [PARENTS], not murder, remain faithful in marriage, not steal, and not tell [LIES]. They must not [COVET] what belonged to their neighbors. The first four commands teach us to love [GOD] and the last six teach us to love other people.",
      "origin": "suggested",
      "teacherReviewRequired": true
    },
